  "details": "Let me explain: I run group instances in popular worlds, and it frequently gets targeted by crashers. Some crashers are popular and for some reason, not removed by vrchat fast enough. Or, I might be running an instance for minors and I REALLY don't want someone showing up as one of the myriad of Epstein or Diddy avatars bc that's...y'know...cringe.\n\nWhat if we were able to create a blacklist or whitelist of disapproved/approved avatars for our groups? Just get the avatar ID and input it into the list to preemptively prevent people from loading in as the avi or turning into it after they join the instance.\n\nIt's significantly less annoying to deal with than having to panic whenever a mod of mine suddenly yells out \"CRASHER ROBOT CRASHER ROBOT CRASHER ROBOT!!!!!\" or have a discussion constantly interrupted by \"DIDDY ALERT!!!\" every five minutes in a Group Public because someone thinks they're funnier than Proximity Chat (you never will be).\n\nIf it's not feasible or if it's flawed, just let me know. But I'd love this to be a feature.",
